From 726ebbeba258aeb601617bfd5700c3c5ab38a9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:13:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] servo: @starting-style, and transitions and animations on
 ::backdrop

@starting-style rules were parsed and cascaded only for Gecko. Servo now
enables them and resolves the starting style of an element, or of one of
its eager pseudo-elements, when it has no previous style or stops being
display: none, and uses it as the before-change style for transitions
(https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions-2/#defining-before-change-style).
Popovers and dialogs, newly inserted elements and their ::backdrop can
then transition in from their @starting-style values as in Chrome.

::backdrop was a lazy pseudo-element, computed afresh by layout every
time, so it had no previous style to transition from and no animation
set. It is now eagerly cascaded like ::before and ::after, but only for
elements in the top layer, and Servo processes its transitions and
animations. An element whose removal from the top layer is deferred by a
transition of overlay is matched as out of it before that transition
applies, so its ::backdrop is resolved again once the transition does,
letting it animate out with the element.

Also moves a doc comment from the previous commit back onto
start_transitions_if_applicable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
